# Root build context for docker/Dockerfile — every target builds from here.
#
# Without this the context is ~2.7 GB (node_modules, .next, the worker venv and
# worktrees/ full of agent checkouts) and, worse, `COPY apps/web/ .` in the
# webbuild stage would bake apps/web/.env.local into an image layer. Deny
# secrets and heavyweight generated trees; everything the Dockerfile actually
# COPYs is listed in the "kept" note at the bottom.

# --- secrets: never in a build context ---
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!config/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- VCS / CI local state ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- dependency + build output trees (re-created inside the image) ---
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.venv
**/.venv-*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# --- runtime + operational data, never part of an image ---
worktrees/
logs/
backups/
*.oci.tar
*.tar.gz
*.log

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Kept deliberately (required by docker/Dockerfile):
#   docker/sourceless.sh   .py -> .pyc for the Pro modules, used in two stages
#   docker/devserver-bootstrap.py
#                          first-start schema apply + settings seed
#   database/migrations/** the schema that bootstrap applies. NOTE: `logs/`
#                          above is root-anchored (Go filepath.Match), so it
#                          does NOT strip apps/web/src/app/api/logs — verified,
#                          not assumed.
#   apps/web/**            source, package.json, package-lock.json, public/, server.ts
#   version.json           read by next.config.ts at build time
#   apps/worker/**         pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/
#   apps/mcp-memory/**     optional Pro MCP server (bracketed COPY tolerates absence)
#   .claude/skills/**      agent skills baked into the worker image
#   docs/assistant/**      Ask Agent knowledge pack
#   scripts/**             maintenance scripts the Ask Agent can propose
